+# ACP Feature Parity: qwen-code in Zedium vs. the first-party Zed agent
+
+**Date:** 2026-06-24
+**Branch:** `feature/acp-subagent-grouping`
+**North star:** the qwen-code (external ACP) experience in the agent panel should match
+what Zed's own native agent gives.
+
+This document is grounded in a live, extensive capture of `qwen --acp` (v0.19.1, OpenRouter
+`qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b`) driven through a battery of feature-exercising prompts, cross-checked
+against the actual Zedium handling code (`acp_thread`, `agent_servers`, `agent_ui`).
+
+Artifacts (committed alongside this doc):
+- `2026-06-24-qwen-acp-extensive-capture.log` — human-readable running transcript of the session.
+- `2026-06-24-qwen-acp-events.jsonl` — full-fidelity, untruncated structured event stream
+  (tool calls, permissions, commands, fs/terminal requests).
+
+## 1. What the capture exercised
+
+One ACP session, seven prompts, deliberately covering distinct protocol surfaces:
+
+| Prompt | Surface exercised | qwen tool / wire |
+|---|---|---|
+| read two files + describe | `read` tool calls, agent text, thinking | `read_file`, `provenance: builtin` |
+| search for "BUG" | `search` tool call, title | `grep_search` |
+| run a shell command | `execute` tool call + **permission** | `run_shell_command` (run **internally**, output as text) |
+| fix a bug | `edit` tool call + **permission** + **diff** content | `edit` → `diff` block |
+| make a 3-step plan | (expected `plan` update) | **plan emitted as plain text — no `plan` update** |
+| delegate to a subagent | subagent tree | `agent` root + `Explore` children (`parentToolCallId`) |
+| use the synonyms skill | `skill` tool call + **permission** | `skill`, `kind: read` |
+
+### What qwen advertised / sent
+
+- **`initialize` →** `agentCapabilities`: `loadSession: true`, `promptCapabilities`
+  `{ image, audio, embeddedContext }`, `sessionCapabilities { list, resume }`,
+  `mcpCapabilities { sse, http }`.
+- **`session/new` →** a `models` block: `currentModelId` + **5 `availableModels`**, each with
+  `_meta.contextLimit`. **No `modes`, no `config_options`.**
+- **`available_commands_update` →** **36 commands**, each with rich `_meta`:
+  `source` (`builtin-command` / `bundled-skill` / `skill-dir-command`), `sourceLabel`
+  (`Built-in` / `Skill` / `Project`), `argumentHint`, `subcommands`, `modelInvocable`. The
+  project skill `synonyms` appears here as a `skill-dir-command`.
+- **Update stream:** `agent_message_chunk` ×1802, `agent_thought_chunk` ×565, `tool_call` ×7,
+  `tool_call_update` ×11, `available_commands_update` ×1. **Zero `plan`, zero
+  `current_mode_update`, zero `UsageUpdate`.**
+- **A proprietary client request:** `craft/drainMidTurnQueue` (qwen extension, not in ACP).
+
+### Two wire facts that matter for correctness
+
+1. **Some tool calls are introduced *only* via `tool_call_update`, never a `tool_call` (new).**
+   The four that needed permission — shell, edit, the subagent root (`agent`), and skill —
+   each arrived first as the `toolCall` embedded in `session/request_permission`, then as a
+   `tool_call_update`. They never got a standalone `tool_call` notification. Zed survives this
+   **only because** `request_tool_call_authorization` → `upsert_tool_call_inner`
+   (`acp_thread.rs:2781`) pre-creates the entry. A `tool_call_update` for a truly unseen id
+   renders a **"Tool call not found"** failed entry (`acp_thread.rs:2504-2527`) — so a provider
+   that updates without either a `tool_call` or a permission request would break. qwen always
+   pairs them, so this is latent, not active.
+2. **The subagent root only ever appears as a `tool_call_update`** (`status: completed`,
+   `title: null`, `_meta {toolName: "agent", provenance: "builtin"}`). Our grouping classifies
+   on both the `tool_call` and `tool_call_update` ingest paths (`acp_thread.rs:2583` and
+   `:2497`), so the root is still recognized. Confirmed against this capture.
+
+## 2. Coverage matrix
+
+✅ correct · 🟡 partial / degraded · ❌ missing · (q) limited by what qwen emits, not by Zed
+
+| ACP surface | qwen sends | Zedium handling | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `agent_message_chunk` (text) | yes (1802) | `push_assistant_content_block` | ✅ |
+| `agent_thought_chunk` | yes (565) | rendered as `<thinking>` | ✅ |
+| `tool_call` / `tool_call_update` | yes | upsert + update, create-on-missing | ✅ |
+| tool `kind`/`status`/`title`/`locations`/`raw_*` | yes | full | ✅ |
+| `ToolCallContent::Diff` | yes (edit) | `Diff::finalized`, smart update | ✅ |
+| `ToolCallContent::Content` (text) | yes (shell, skill, summary) | rendered as markdown | ✅ |
+| **Subagent grouping** | parent-pointer tree | **this branch: card + pop-out** | ✅ (was ❌) |
+| `session/request_permission` | yes (4×) | flat/dropdown/patterns | ✅ |
+| `fs/read_text_file` / `write_text_file` | yes | handled | ✅ |
+| `available_commands_update` | 36, rich `_meta` | stored; only Zed's own `category` meta used | 🟡 **skill/source/argumentHint/subcommands dropped** |
+| **`models` in `session/new`** | 5 models + ctx limits | **`response.models` referenced 0×; no `model_selector` for `AcpConnection`** | ❌ **no model picker for external agents** |
+| `plan` update | — (text only) | `update_plan` exists | ❌ (q) qwen never emits it |
+| terminal (`terminal/create` + `Terminal` content) | — (shell run internally) | fully implemented | 🟡 (q) shell shows as a text blob, not a live terminal |
+| `current_mode_update` / session modes | — | handled (native uses it) | (q) qwen doesn't use modes |
+| `UsageUpdate` / token meter | — | handled | (q) qwen doesn't emit usage |
+| `craft/drainMidTurnQueue` | yes | unregistered → method-not-found | ❌ qwen-proprietary; mid-turn queue disabled |
+| Audio content blocks | capability only | `.audio(true)` advertised but **dropped** (no match arm, `acp_thread.rs:1265`) | 🟡 latent |
+| Image content blocks | capability only | decoded; some paths render `` `Image` `` placeholder | 🟡 |
+| `availableModels[_meta].contextLimit` | yes | ignored | 🟡 minor |
+
+## 3. Gaps, ranked toward native parity
+
+The gaps split into **(A) Zed under-consumes what qwen sends** (actionable in Zedium) and
+**(B) qwen under-sends vs. native** (not fixable from Zed alone).
+
+### A. Actionable in Zedium
+
+1. **Subagent transcripts — FIXED on this branch.** Was the worst gap: every subagent step
+   landed flat in main with no separate transcript. Now grouped into a card with a recursive
+   pop-out (`SubagentGrouping` + `SubagentIndex`, qwen adapter). This was the original mandate.
+
+2. **No model picker for external ACP agents.** qwen advertises 5 models with a current
+   selection in `session/new`, and ACP supports switching, but `AcpConnection` never reads
+   `response.models` and does not implement `model_selector` (`connection.rs:219` default
+   `None`). The native agent does (`agent/src/agent.rs:2552`), so it gets the picker and qwen
+   doesn't. **This is the highest-value remaining parity gap.** Fix shape: implement
+   `AgentModelSelector` for `AcpConnection`, populated from `session/new`'s `models` and
+   updated via ACP `session/set_model`, then surface the existing model-selector UI.
+
+3. **Slash-command / skill metadata is thrown away.** qwen sends `source` / `sourceLabel`
+   (`Built-in` / `Skill` / `Project`), `argumentHint`, `subcommands`, and `modelInvocable` per
+   command; Zed consumes only its own native `category` meta key
+   (`COMMAND_CATEGORY_META_KEY`). Consequences in the palette: skills are indistinguishable
+   from built-ins, no argument hints, no subcommand affordances, no source grouping. Fix shape:
+   map qwen's `source`/`sourceLabel` into the command-category grouping and thread
+   `argumentHint`/`subcommands` into the command UI.
+
+4. **`craft/drainMidTurnQueue` returns method-not-found.** A qwen extension for draining
+   mid-turn queued messages. Low priority and proprietary, but it's why "type-ahead while the
+   agent works" likely won't behave the same as in qwen's own UI. Document as known-unsupported.
+
+5. **Audio content blocks are silently dropped** despite `.audio(true)` being advertised
+   (`acp_thread.rs:1265` has no `Audio` arm). Either stop advertising the capability or add a
+   placeholder. Latent today (qwen sent no audio), but it's a self-inconsistency.
+
+### B. Limited by what qwen emits (not Zed bugs)
+
+6. **No plan/todo tracker for qwen.** qwen answers "make a plan" with prose in
+   `agent_message_chunk`, never a `plan` session update, so Zed's plan UI (which works for
+   native) never appears. Nothing to fix in Zed; note it as an experience gap inherent to this
+   provider.
+
+7. **Shell is a text blob, not a live terminal.** qwen runs `run_shell_command` in-process and
+   reports a formatted `content/text` block (`Command/Directory/Output/Exit Code/...`); it
+   never calls `terminal/create`. Zed's full terminal-embedding path therefore never engages
+   for qwen. Renders fine, but without streaming/scrollback/kill affordances the native agent
+   gets.
+
+8. **Session modes & usage meter** — qwen emits neither `current_mode_update` nor
+   `UsageUpdate`, so the mode switcher and token meter stay dark for qwen. Provider-side.
+
+## 4. Honesty notes
+
+- The capture is real and reproducible (harness: `scratchpad/acp_probe2.py`). Counts and
+  `_meta` shapes are taken directly from the wire, not inferred.
+- All Zed-side verdicts are cited to code read on this branch. The subagent-grouping ✅ is
+  logic- and compile-verified and now also cross-checked against this capture's exact wire
+  shape (root-only-via-update, children-via-new); it has **not** been visually verified in a
+  running GUI in this pass (the user is doing that build separately).
+- Gap #2 (model picker) and #3 (command metadata) are confirmed by code inspection
+  (`response.models` referenced 0×; no `model_selector` for `AcpConnection`) but no fix has
+  been attempted here — this document is analysis, not implementation.
